From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nix-on-droid <nix-on-droid@local>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] path: report the real errno from substitute_binding_stat

Ports proot-me/proot d2428af: the function collapsed every access
failure to -ENOENT.  Report the real errno instead, so guests observe
faithful errors (EACCES on an unreadable parent, ENOENT on a missing
component, ...).

Two details this fork needs on top of upstream:

- The failure must be captured right after the stat call: build_glue()
  below runs further syscalls (mkdir/mknod/mkdtemp) that clobber errno,
  so `return -errno` at the end would report the wrong cause.
- A build_glue() failure used to become a bare -1, which is not a valid
  -errno and reaches the guest as EPERM; take its errno (or -EIO when
  it left errno at zero).

The f2fs skip branch reports ENOENT explicitly for the same reason.

NOTE: must be applied after android-seccomp-self-compat.patch, which
renames the stat call to ac_lstat(); the context below matches that.

---
 src/path/canon.c |   21 ++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/path/canon.c b/src/path/canon.c
--- a/src/path/canon.c
+++ b/src/path/canon.c
@@ -155,8 +155,13 @@ static inline int substitute_binding_stat(Tracee *tracee, Finality finality, uns
 	statl.st_mode = 0;
 	if (should_skip_file_access_due_to_f2fs_bug(tracee, host_path)) {
 		status = -ENOENT;
+		errno = ENOENT;
 	} else {
 		status = ac_lstat(host_path, &statl);
+		/* Save the stat failure before build_glue() below runs more
+		 * syscalls that would clobber errno. */
+		if (status < 0)
+			status = -errno;
 		/* /linkerconfig directory is present and accessible on Android,
 		 * but cannot be stat()'d, use hardcoded stat if access was denied
 		 *
@@ -172,16 +177,18 @@ static inline int substitute_binding_stat(Tracee *tracee, Finality finality, uns
 	 * the initialization of a binding.  */
 	if (status < 0 && tracee->glue_type != 0) {
 		statl.st_mode = build_glue(tracee, guest_path, host_path, finality);
-		if (statl.st_mode == 0)
-			status = -1;
+		if (statl.st_mode == 0) {
+			/* build_glue() failed: report its errno, not the
+			 * bare -1 (which is not a valid -errno). */
+			status = (errno != 0 ? -errno : -EIO);
+		}
 	}
 
-	/* Return an error if a non-final component isn't a
-	 * directory nor a symlink.  The error is "No such
-	 * file or directory" if this component doesn't exist,
-	 * otherwise the error is "Not a directory".  */
+	/* Return an error if a non-final component isn't a directory
+	 * nor a symlink.  status already carries the negative errno from
+	 * above (lstat failure, or the glue failure).  */
 	if (!IS_FINAL(finality) && !S_ISDIR(statl.st_mode) && !S_ISLNK(statl.st_mode))
-		return (status < 0 ? -ENOENT : -ENOTDIR);
+		return (status < 0 ? status : -ENOTDIR);
 
 	return (S_ISLNK(statl.st_mode) ? 1 : 0);
 }
--
